# 0104-shader-cache-check-fast-prep-xlate-gc.patch -- speed-up items W2, W3, W4 (app side), B2 (app side) and B9 (app side) of the owner's list: the warm-up knows when iOS emptied its
# Metal shader cache, may use the device's compiler concurrency, compiles for size like the host; the translator's GC cost is logged; an experimental translator switch. Applies after 0103.
#
# W2 -- "Check the shader cache" (Settings > Build, on by default; shader_cache_check 1/0 in Documents/gameapp.settings.tsv).
#   WHY: iOS's Metal shader cache (about 255 MB) is emptied at a reboot, a reinstall and an iOS update (developer.apple.com/forums/thread/659856). The warm-up's markers (warmed.tsv,
#     prepared.tsv: GameWarmLogic.Header) named only the app build and the chain, so after a reboot a game stayed "prepared" and its first Play compiled cold (1,061-1,708 s measured).
#   FIX (GameAppWarm.cs ShaderCacheCheck, GameWarm.MarkerHeader / WrittenHeader / CheckCacheOnce):
#     * the markers' first line now also names the boot and the OS build: "# warmed app_build <b> chain <c> boot <kern.boottime seconds> os <kern.osversion>", always WRITTEN with them.
#       With the check on, ParseWarmed / PreparedMatches (ShaderCacheCheck.Holds) refuse a marker of another boot (more than 120 s apart: iOS moves kern.boottime when it steps the clock)
#       or OS build, or one written before 0104; off, only the app build and the chain count, as before. FirstStartPending, the queue's counts and the game sheet's "Shaders prepared" use it.
#     * the probe: once per process and game (the queue's sync at a launch or a return, while nothing else has the phone and no run goes; and a run's own start, also in an exported app),
#       the first 3 libraries warmed.tsv says were COMPILED are compiled again with WarmCompile and timed; every one above 50 ms = cold: warmed.tsv goes back to its header, prepared.tsv is
#       removed, the game is prepared again; games/<id>/cache_probe.tsv keeps the epoch of that reset, so a game found cold AGAIN in the same boot is not reset again (iOS may simply not keep
#       its libraries). cache_probe.tsv is cache state: never exported (PlayerWarm.CacheState).
#     * every decision is one log line "shader cache: <title>: ...": prepared before the phone restarted / iOS was updated (23A341 to 23B82) / before the check; probed warm (times);
#       probed cold (times), markers reset; cold again, not reset; nothing decided.
# W3 -- "Faster shader preparation" (Settings > Build, off by default; shader_prep_fast 1/0).
#   FIX (GameAppWarm.cs FastWarm): on, with "Shader preparation" at Auto, in the foreground at thermal Nominal or Fair: as many workers as MTLDevice.MaximumConcurrentCompilationTaskCount
#     (the .NET binding: IMTLDevice.MaximumConcurrentCompilationTaskCount, nuint, iOS 26.1+; 0 before: Auto's count), capped at the phone's cores; in the background on a charger: Utility
#     QoS instead of Background (still one worker). Kept: none at thermal Serious or Critical (a charger does not lift it), one in the background, a core count chosen in "Shader
#     preparation" wins. The automatic run starts threads for the device's limit (the extra ones wait while it is off), so a switch applies to the run that is going.
#     The phone's charging state: UIDevice.BatteryState (its notification), on the main thread.
# W4 -- WarmCompile compiles for size: MTLCompileOptions.OptimizationLevel = MTLLibraryOptimizationLevel.Size, always (engine-patches/0535 sets the same in the host's src_compile).
#   WarmCompile's options are now, in full: OptimizationLevel Size, MathMode Relaxed (iOS 18+, always here), PreserveInvariance true, LanguageVersion 4.0 only for a source containing
#   "vertex_value<" (iOS 26+), else the default; nothing else set (no macros, no install name, no libraries, the default library type).
# B2 -- the translator's GC cost (GameAppField.cs TranslatorGc, GameAppMain.cs): at the end of each chain run of a build (not a Play), one line
#   "translator GC: gen0 N, gen1 N, gen2 N (F forced, X s), paused Y s, T translations": the deltas of GC.CollectionCount(0/1/2) and GC.GetTotalPauseDuration() over the chain run
#   (process-wide counts; the translator is what allocates then), the compacting collections XlateEntry forces itself and their own time (timed there: the runtime may report no pause,
#   then "paused n/a"). No line when the run translated nothing.
# B9 -- "Optimized translator (experimental)" (Settings > Build, off by default): saved as xlate_optimized 1/0 (GameAppUi.XlateOptimizedOn); the chain reads the key at each build (the
#   Rust side, not in this patch). The change is said in the log ("build setting: optimized translator (experimental) on: ...; it applies to the next build ...").
# The three switches sit in the Settings shelf's Build card after "Low performance" (GameAppShelf.cs), and in the older Build section (GameAppMain.cs BuildSection) after its own.
# VERIFIED (2026-11-23, M1 Pro): every patch 0010-0104 applies in order (scripts/check-patches-apply.sh); compile only (dotnet build -c Release -r ios-arm64 -t:Compile on the last device
#   build's generated project): 0 errors, the same warnings per file and code as without 0104. The pure parts (ShaderCacheCheck, FastWarm, GameWarmLogic's header checks) compiled on the
#   Mac with WARM_LOGIC_ONLY: 51 checks pass (same boot, a 90 s clock step, a reboot, an iOS update, a pre-0104 marker, check off; the probe's rows and verdict, the reset guard; the worker
#   counts and the QoS rule); the sysctl reads (kern.boottime as a 16-byte timeval, kern.osversion) and the GC line, on the Mac.
# NOT VERIFIED: anything on an iPhone: the boot time and OS build read there, the probe's times (cache hit vs cold), the reset after a real reboot, MaximumConcurrentCompilationTaskCount's
#   value, the speed and heat of the faster preparation, the GC line's numbers, the switches' layout. Whether Metal's cache really keys on optimizationLevel on iOS is measured on the Mac only
#   (engine-patches/0535).
# NEW STRINGS: "Check the shader cache", "iOS empties its shader cache when the phone restarts or iOS is updated. ...", "shader cache: ", "iOS emptied its shader cache since, so the game
#   is prepared again", " prepared libraries compiled again in ", "the preparation stands", "Faster shader preparation", "Compiles as many shaders at once as the phone allows ...",
#   "faster shader preparation on", "Optimized translator (experimental)", "Smaller and faster shaders, but experimental: ...", "build setting: optimized translator (experimental) ",
#   "translator GC: gen0 ".
